      <div type="clause" n="47.2">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:LeisWl">Leis Wl</ref> 47.2</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" corresp="#wit-i"><pb n="519" ed="#liebermann"/>E si nul parent<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#LeisWl_47-2.lnote.oe.1"/> n’ami<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#LeisWl_47-2.lnote.oe.2"/> ceste justise deforcent, seient forfeit<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#LeisWl_47-2.lnote.oe.3"/> envers l[e<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#LeisWl_47-2.lnote.oe.4"/>] rei de VI lib.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" corresp="#wit-l"><pb n="519" ed="#liebermann"/>Quodsi amicorum aliquis hanc iusticiam difforciat, sit in forisfactura VI librarum uersus regem.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="xno" source="#robertson" n="47.2" corresp="#wit-i"><pb n="274" ed="#robertson"/>E si nul parent n'ami ceste justise deforcent, seint forfeit envers l[e] rei de VI lib.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="519" ed="#liebermann"/>47, 2. Und wenn irgend ein Verwandter oder Freund [des Verbrechers] diesen Rechtsvollzug gewaltsam hindern, seien sie gegenüber dem König in Strafgeld von 6<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="a" target="#LeisWl_47-2.lnote.de1.a"/> £ [Silber] verfallen.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">47, 2. And if any kinsman or friend [of the criminal] forcibly hinder this execution of the law, they shall have incurred towards the king a money penalty of 6 £ [of silver].</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-i"><pb n="275" ed="#robertson"/>And if any relative or friend opposes by force this exercise of justice, he shall pay a fine of £6 to the King.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#liebermann" n="519"><ref target="clause:IICn_25-2">II Cn 25.2</ref></note>
        <note type="comparisonPrinted" source="#liebermann">II Cn. 25, 2</note>
        <note type="editorial">Added October 2026 from Robertson pp. 274–275 (text and translation); Liebermann’s text and German translation added from Gesetze I p. 519, October 2026 (two independent readings of the page images)</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_47-2.lnote.oe.1" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">519</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">per. <hi rend="italic">Im</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">per. Im</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_47-2.lnote.oe.2" n="2" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">519</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">besere</hi> u ami?</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">read u ami?</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_47-2.lnote.oe.3" n="3" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">519</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">fehlt Im</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">omitted in Im</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_47-2.lnote.oe.4" n="4" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">519</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">li <hi rend="italic">I</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">li I</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="translationFootnote" xml:id="LeisWl_47-2.lnote.de1.a" n="a" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">519</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">s. o.</hi> 42, 1ᵉ</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">see above 42, 1ᵉ</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="LeisWl_47-2.lnote.de._" n="-" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">292</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">‘Verweigerung des Zuges’ zur Bestrafung und 120 Schill. Strafgeld bietet Cnut, wovon dies vielleicht nur aus Flüchtigkeit abweicht; <hi rend="italic">s. o</hi>. 42, 1{1}; <hi rend="italic">Gl</hi> Strafgeldfixum 18</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Cnut has ‘refusal to join the expedition’ to punish [the offender] and a fine of 120 shill., from which this perhaps departs only through carelessness; <hi rend="italic">see above</hi> 42, 1{1}; <hi rend="italic">Gl</hi> Strafgeldfixum 18</seg></note>
      </div>
    </body>
